{"id": "EUVD-2026-95793", "enisaUuid": "5d9cf886-fb24-38dc-a159-19a1d306225c", "description": "Open5GS through 2.8.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in ogs_pfcp_parse_volume_measurement() in lib/pfcp/types.c that allows remote unauthenticated attackers to read past IE buffers. Attackers can send a PFCP Session Report Request to the SMF on UDP port 8805 with a short, all-flags Volume Measurement IE, reading up to 48 bytes and potentially crashing the SMF.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T14:08:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T14:44:45", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/commit/88e64fc1f87e0d321364b3bb710ef6a8f274e568", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/security/advisories/GHSA-37c3-hv4f-688p", "https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/blob/v2.8.0/lib/pfcp/types.c#L581-L635", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/open5gs-through-2.8.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-pfcp-volume-measurement-ie"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108102", "GHSA-337v-466h-8gh6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08a4dea5-fc6e-3449-bf2a-6a53cde73f43", "product": {"name": "Open5GS", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e7757a63-5714-35bd-a788-fa28cf4012a8", "vendor": {"name": "Open5GS"}}], "isExploited": false}